*Heading
Solid reference for coupling_shell_plate.inp: the plate as C3D20R bricks under *Rigid Body
** The same 100 x 40 x 2 plate, 10 x 4 C3D20R elements with one through the thickness (the
** brick ccx expands an S8R into), clamped at x = 0.  The x = 100 end face moves rigidly
** with RP = (120, 20, 5), which carries the same force and moment.  ccx accepts a rigid
** body on solid nodes, so this deck needs no knots; validate_with_ccx.py compares the RP
** displacements of the two decks.
